  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SJO ODA 2025</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project seeks to integrate the experience gained by organizations in the Honduran financial system, which have implemented the SARAS environmental and social risk management system since 2021. This process incorporates the Green Taxonomy, which was approved in the Central American region in November 2024 and is expected to be approved in Honduras in November 2025. The project will systematize this relationship and develop a guide that will promote the creation of new financial products based on a Green Taxonomy approach and encourage stakeholders from four productive sectors to submit investment projects that are eligible for the new taxonomy.
The expected results are:
1) A knowledge product titled Gu&#xed;a para la Financiaci&#xf3;n Sostenible de Proyectos con Taxonom&#xed;a Verde?, useful for stimulating the financial market toward sustainable solutions. 
2) A model for managing the financing of productive sectors based on regulatory and complementary requirements established by the green taxonomy. 
3) Four case studies on the experience of sustainable financing using green taxonomy applied in the financial system and the productive sector.</narrative>
  </description>
